00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.990 align:start position:0%
 
hello and welcome to my latest uh  leaders briefing it's December now so  I'm we're all on the countdown to  Christmas and I hope you're looking  forward to uh to spending a bit of time  with your family and enjoying some  delicious turkey and opening a few  presents I know we all are here at  Northeast Derbyshire District Council  um Christmas we know is also a really  hard time for some of our families and  even more so at the moment as we're  going through the cost of living crisis  hopefully you've seen from our last  leaders briefing and from our Northeast  harborshire news and our website that  we're doing a lot of work at the moment  to try and support our residents and our  businesses and and communities and and  all of our all of our population around  um dealing with the impacts of the cost  of living crisis whether that's in terms  of energy saving advice helping you to  sort of manage your bills or signposting  people to other forms of community  support or really explaining some of the  government support that's out there and  trying to help people to access that um  and another thing that we've recently  done as a council is commit to employing  two new community outreach workers whose  job it will be to go out into the  community and to support residents  particularly those who are particularly  struggling at the moment into accessing  some of that additional support and to  help them in terms of managing finances  so we're really pleased about that it's  a really important part of being able to  support Northeast Derbyshire through the  cost of living crisis and our key  message to all of our communities and  all of our residences if you or anyone  you know needs our support or needs any  help whatsoever please don't hesitate to  get in touch don't leave it in too long  just get in touch with us and we'll do  whatever we can to support you and we  stand ready to support everyone who  needs it through this difficult period  that we're going through now the  Northeast aubergine news magazine also  includes lots of other handy tips over  the over the festive period things like  our opening times both the district  council building here at Mill Lane and  our Leisure centers who obviously some  changes to opening times over that  Christmas period but also in terms of  the the bin Collections and we'll all be  aware that green bean collections have  been suspended over the winter period  and we know that obviously Christmas is  a time with lots of wrapping paper and  presents and recycling so there's also  some information there in the in the  news magazine about how to deal your  recycling and also who to contact in the  case of an emergency situation where you  need the district council's help  particularly during those periods where  we're closed down so do check out the  the news magazine there's lots of useful  handy tips there that'll hopefully help  Christmas be as smooth as it possibly  can now we know that Christmas is also a  time when unfortunately some people  choose to take advantage so there's lots  of useful information on our website  about how to protect yourself from  burglaries which can be so disheartening  and so upsetting for families during the  Christmas period there's loads of  information on our website so do check  it out about keeping yourself safe and  keeping all of your Christmas  possessions safe during this during this  winter period  now moving on to a bit of different news  the government have recently launched a  uk-wide veterans survey and we're  encouraging all veterans within the  Northeast Derbyshire area to contribute  to that and go online and and fill it  out it's running for about 12 weeks  starting in November so it's still got a  bit of time to to complete that if you  haven't yet already and it's all about  the government listening to and hearing  from the experiences of veterans around  the services that we provide and and the  support that's out there and available  to them so please do go on the go on the  website the government's website and and  fill in the survey if you are a veteran  in Northeast Derbyshire  and again sticking with the theme of  veterans we recently were awarded the  Armed Forces Gold Award as part of the  Armed Forces Covenant and you might be  aware of this from previous leaders  briefings we're one of only about 630  Employers in the whole country out of  about 7 million employers who've been  awarded this really prestigious award by  the ministry of defense and our Armed  Forces Champion councilor Martin Thacker  recently was presented with the award by  Bruce Spencer who's the regional  coordinator for the scheme working for  the ministry of Defense it's a great  achievement for the council we're really  really proud of it and it's really  Testament to our real commitment to  supporting those in the armed forces for  a reservist and obviously for Veterans  as well so really proud of that and  obviously we hope to continue to  maintain that high level of standard in  terms of service to those people moving  on again we're also offering some free  digital training to over 50s at the  moment so if you or anyone you know  might be interested in that and finding  out more please go on our website it's  as I say it's free and it never hurts to  brush up on your skills particularly in  this very digital world that we're  living in now so please do check it out  I think it's a great opportunity and  hopefully lots of residents over 50s in  particular in Northeast Derbyshire will  make good use of that from some of my  recent leaders briefings you'll be aware  of the the moves I thought at the moment  towards the Devolution deal for the East  Midlands so this is about  Nottinghamshire and Nottingham City and  Derbyshire and Derby City working  together to get a Devolution deal from  the government which could mean  substantial investment in the region and  having an elected mayor to cover that  whole area there's a consultation that's  currently out at the moment it runs for  several weeks into the new year so  please go on the the website the East  Midlands Devolution deal consultation  website to give your views on on what  you think that might mean for the region  now a bit of breaking news now is that  we've just found out from the government  that we've been awarded our 2.58 million  pounds from the UK shared Prosperity  fund now again I've probably referred to  this in previous leaders briefings but  this is a funding from the government  following the our departure from the  European Union and it's all about  investing in communities it's about  we're using our uh our pot for Northeast  Derbyshire if you like to support things  like investing in parks and play areas  improving shop Frontage improving  Village Hall facilities helping people  with skills and trying to support people  getting into work so it's all those  sorts of things we we have a lot of  flexibility around how we want to use  that and in North East Derbyshire we've  tried to focus it on really visible  things that people will see as  improvements in their community and  that's absolutely the right thing to do  and we're really pleased to have that  funding now confirmed by the government  and hopefully you'll see start to see  some of those improvements happening  over the next over the few months and  years it's a three-year deal so it will  take time to deliver but yeah we're  really pleased to be able to get  cracking now and and get starting in  terms of investing into some of our  really important Community projects  another really key project for us is the  rebuild of Charlie Park Leisure Center  now you'll know from previous leaders  briefings again that this has been a big  project for us we've already approved  the budget for it it's it's a 23 million  pound project involving quite a  significant Council investment but also  we've got funding from the claycross  town deal and from other partners like  sport England which we're trying to  secure at the moment and so we've got  the project all been lined up it's gone  through the planning process and now  we're very very close now literally  within the next few days to signing the  contract and that means that work will  hopefully start quite early on in the  New Year sort of January February time  we'll start to see a bit more activity  on site and I know for lots of residents  in Clay Cross they've heard about this  scheme for a long long time and I think  the the general perception is that we  keep hearing about it but it's not  happening yet well now now we're in the  stage finally where actually you're  going to start out seeing some of the  works on the ground and I think that's  really important demonstration of our  commitment to deliver this vital project  and look forward to seeing it come to  fruition it's not going to be a quick  process it's still going to take almost  two years to deliver the new Leisure  Center but I'm really excited about  seeing it when it's done because I've  seen from the visuals that it looks  absolutely fantastic and it's going to  make such a difference to all the  residents in Clay Cross and The Wider  Villages that that Charlie Park serves  now one of the issues that I know is a  key concern for a lot of residents in  Northeast Derbyshire is the issue of  fracking now you'll probably hopefully  be aware that there was a moratorium  introduced by the government which  essentially banned fracking it stopped  fracking from happening anywhere in the  country that was introduced in 2019  however following some of the changes in  government recently fracking was put for  a short period of time back on the table  now that Rishi sunax in in post the  moratorium has been put back in place  and that means very clearly that there  will be no fracking applications coming  forward in Northeast Derbyshire but I'm  really pleased that as a council we've  unanimously on a sort of cross-party  basis agreed a recent council meeting  that we would reaffirm our commitment to  opposing any fracking in Northeast  Derbyshire should it ever come back onto  the table and I'm really pleased that we  could vote together as you know speak  with one voice on that issue because I  know how important it is for so many of  our communities in terms of that fear  that it might happen again so we've got  good news in terms of the moratorium  back in place and I just want to  reassure everyone of Northeast  Derbyshire District council's commitment  to oppose it should it ever come back on  the table  one of the other things that I've been  doing recently is spending a bit more  time back to the floor with some of our  staff around different services within  the council so you'll be aware hopefully  that earlier in the year myself and the  deputy leader of the council councilor  Charlotte keep it spent a shift each  with some of our refuse teams both in  the North and the South of the district  you know emptying bins and I really  enjoyed the experience and and learned a  lot about the work that they do day in  day out to keep keep the district moving  really and you know how how lost we  would be without them so as well as  spending some time out on the bins I  also recently went to dronfield sports  center for a morning and spent the  morning with staff learning a bit more  about how the Leisure centers operate I  did a backwash on one of the pools and  did some health and safety checks and  also spent some time with some of the  lifeguards doing a uh doing a mock  Theory exam which I'm afraid to say I  didn't pass unfortunately but no it's  really great to spend that time with the  Leisure service and understand a bit  more about their work and and about how  the Leisure centers operate and I really  did leave feeling like they they run  like a really well-oiled machine I was  really assured in terms of the work that  they do to support each other okay  finally all that's left me to do is to  say please do continue checking our  website and our social media channels  and also the Northeast Derbyshire news  magazine for all the latest news and  information and how to get in touch with  us and all I can say is uh I wish you  all a very merry Christmas and a happy  New Year and a huge thank you to all of  our residents and our businesses and  really importantly all of our staff here  at Northeast Derbyshire District Council  have a well-deserved break and I look  forward to seeing you in the new year  foreign

